{
  "hook": "validate-skill-paths",
  "_notes": [
    "PostToolUse hook. Two observable outcomes only: silent exit 0, or a PostToolUse",
    "additionalContext JSON report on stdout (still exit 0). The source has NO deny path — no",
    "deny(...) and no \"deny\" anywhere — so there is no deny case to write; every case is 'allow'",
    "(silent) or 'context' (report emitted).",
    "Every path in stdin is RELATIVE on purpose: the hook re-reads the edited file from disk and",
    "resolves ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}/${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} against the discovered plugin root, so the",
    "fixture must live at the path stdin names. The harness runs both implementations at the same",
    "sandbox cwd, so relative paths resolve into the fixture and the emitted report (which embeds the",
    "resolved path verbatim) is comparable. Absolute paths would be unwritable from a golden file.",
    "find_plugin_root walks up from the file and stops at the sandbox root, where the fixture puts",
    ".claude-plugin/plugin.json, so plugin_root == Path('.') and the report's rel path is the",
    "sandbox-relative one.",
    "Silent branches covered: non-Edit/Write tool, missing file_path, non-.md suffix, no plugin root,",
    "unreadable file, and a file whose refs all resolve / are skipped. Report branches covered:",
    "broken ${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR} ref, broken ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT} ref, skill dir inferred by walking",
    "up to the nearest SKILL.md, the !`cat` multi-argument extraction+dedup ordering, and the",
    "FENCED_BANG_BACKTICK danger path (which fires even when the referenced file exists)."
  ],
